.TH FILI-ARCHIVE 1 "" "fili-archive" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fili-archive, archiveur \- compress and extract files (Archiveur)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fili-archive pack
[\fB\-f\fR \fIFORMAT\fR] [\fB\-l\fR \fILEVEL\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-hidden\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-q\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR] \fIFILE\fR...
.br
.B fili-archive unpack
[\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIFOLDER\fR] \fIARCHIVE\fR...
.br
.B fili-archive open
\fIARCHIVE\fR...
.br
.B fili-archive list
\fIARCHIVE\fR
.br
.B fili-archive about
.SH DESCRIPTION
Archiveur is the display name of \fBfili-archive\fR; \fBarchiveur\fR is the same command. Both are other names of the \fBfili-file\fR program (Casier), which runs as Archiveur under these names. It has no window: it compresses
and extracts with \fBtar\fR, \fBzip\fR and \fB7z\fR, which must be installed. It is meant to be called by a file manager, a
file association or a script.
.PP
It never overwrites anything ("Archive 2.zip", "folder 2"), and the result only appears once it is finished: a failure or
an interruption leaves nothing half done. The created paths are printed, one per line. Outside a terminal the result is
announced with \fBnotify-send\fR. When the Filigrane \fBfili-tx\fR is installed, every call is a transaction that
\fBfili-tx undo\fR reverses.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B pack
Create an archive next to the files (zip by default).
.TP
.B unpack, extract
Extract next to the archive, or into \fIFOLDER\fR. A single item at the top of the archive is put down as it is,
otherwise the contents go into a folder named after the archive.
.TP
.B open
Same as \fBunpack\fR (file association).
.TP
.B list
Show the contents of an archive.
.TP
.B about
Version, commands and what Archiveur is made of.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
zip (default), 7z, tar.gz, tar.xz or tar.zst.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR
fast, normal (default) or best.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-hidden\fR
Leave hidden files out.
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
The password is the first line of standard input (AES\-256 zip or 7z with encrypted names). It is never an argument.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
The archive to create (pack; the format follows its extension), or the folder to extract into (unpack).
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
No transaction and no notification, for a caller with its own panel and undo.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FILI_ARCHIVE_FORMAT
Default format of \fBpack\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when something failed, 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
tar(1), zip(1), 7z(1)
